vulkan-game: one client source and one server source

Application implementations stay in server/server.cpp and client/client.cpp.
Each non-game namespace has a matching declaration header in its own folder;
inline helpers and function bodies remain in the existing .cpp sources.
The game:: and game_weapons namespaces remain inside the source files.
The client includes the shared portion of the server source; these are the
only two application translation units. Shaders and game assets stay at the
repository root, so runtime paths are unchanged.

VulkanWrapper, VulkanSystems and Vulkan-Headers are pinned Git submodules.
The game build reuses the PCloud integration supplied by VulkanSystems for
GPU, Render, BVH, Spatial, Jobs, PCloud and their shaders. Network and Editor
are compiled locally from that same submodule. GLFW (window/input), fastgltf
(GLB import), Ozz (animation), stb (images), and Mbed TLS (DTLS) are still
required third-party dependencies, handled by c.

First build after cloning:
  git submodule update --init --recursive
  c build vulkan-server
  c build vulkan-client

Run from the repository root:
  c build run vulkan-server
  c build run vulkan-client

The previous source layout and build were runtime-tested. After this
reorganization, compile and runtime verification are required again.
